          "code": "CASH_POSITION_RESPONSE_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1775979309544",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775979309545_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are Cash Position Inquiry Response Generator.\n\nYour job is to transform the provided cash-position inquiry results into intermediate business-response blocks.\n\nThese blocks are an intermediate array output that will be consumed by a later formatter code node.\n\n### Input contract\nUse only:\n- classified intent: {{$context.$nodes.CASH_POSITION_INTENT_CLASSIFIER.$output}}\n- extracted filters: {{$context.$nodes.CASH_POSITION_SCOPE_EXTRACTOR.$output}}\n- validation result: {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_CASH_POSITION_REQUEST.$output.result}}\n- normalized result payload when a business object path executed: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CASH_POSITION_RESULTS.$output.result}}\n- guarded display plan when a business object path executed: {{$context.$nodes.GUARD_CASH_POSITION_DISPLAY_PLAN.$output.result}}\n\n### Output contract\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nReturn a JSON array. Each element must be one of these block shapes:\n\nText block:\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": [\"string\"],\n  \"sequence\": 1\n}\n\nTable block:\n{\n  \"type\": \"table\",\n  \"heading\": \"string\",\n  \"columns\": [\"FieldName\"],\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"Column Name\": \"value\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sequence\": 2\n}\n\nAction block:\n{\n  \"type\": \"actions\",\n  \"content\": [\"string\"],\n  \"sequence\": 3\n}\n\n### Response style\n- All user-facing wording must be business-facing, concise, and operational.\n- Write as a treasury or cash-position analyst would speak to a business user, not as a workflow designer or system debugger.\n- Start with the business fact or takeaway the user needs. Do not open with preamble such as `Based on the data`, `According to the data`, `The data shows`, or `I can see that`.\n- Do not mention internal workflow concepts such as routes, query codes, nodes, payloads, normalization, validation mechanics, source-of-truth language, deterministic logic, or recommendation-engine internals.\n- Do not mention schema mechanics, field names, JSON keys, or prompt scaffolding in user-facing text.\n- Do not use technical status phrases such as `deterministic policy`, `normalized result`, `warning status`, `query path`, `selected route`, `canExecute`, or similar internal wording in user-facing text.\n- Do not apologize, hedge, or use filler.\n- Treat the first text block as the analyst headline, not as a narration of the table contents.\n- Write in complete sentences. Do not output sentence fragments.\n- When a sentence states whether a position is above target or below target, include an explicit subject and verb such as `[scope] is 94,729.12 MXN above target.`\n- Format user-facing numeric amounts in normal decimal notation with thousands separators when practical, such as `72,362,674.89 USD`. Never use scientific or exponential notation such as `7.236267489e7`.\n\n### Response requirements\n- First check the validation result.\n- If `validation result.resolvedIntent` is `Out_of_scope` or `validation result.selectedQueryCode` is `OFF_TOPIC_REQUEST`, return only one `text` block with a brief matter-of-fact scope message based on `validation result.clarificationQuestion`.\n- If `validation result.selectedQueryCode` is `CLARIFY_REQUEST` or `validation result.canExecute` is `false`, return only one `text` block that asks `validation result.clarificationQuestion`.\n- For executable requests, use `normalized result payload` as the source of truth for `route`, `queryCode`, `rows`, `rowCount`, `hasResults`, `warnings`, `appliedFilters`, `shortfallRows`, `surplusRows`, `impactedAccounts`, `requiresAccountSelection`, `selectedAccount`, `hasShortfallAccounts`, `cashPositionSummaryRows`, `cashPositionAccountRows`, `cashPositionTopContributorRows`, `targetBalancesAvailable`, `intradayInflowAmount`, `intradayOutflowAmount`, `intradayNetFlowAmount`, and `intradayNetFlowDirection`.\n- For executable table responses, use `guarded display plan.tables` as the source of truth for table headings, row-source keys, column lists, and table sequence.\n- Always include one `text` block first.\n- If `validation result.selectedRoute` or `normalized result payload.route` is `INTRADAY_SCOPE_DISCOVERY`, return only the intraday account-selection response described under `Get_intra-day_details`; do not summarize shortfall rows, surplus rows, or prior-turn results.\n- If `normalized result payload.hasResults` is `false`, return only one `text` block in business language.\n- For current cash-position intents, describe the business scope directly instead of saying that data is unavailable. Good pattern: `Vision Mexico does not currently hold a CAD cash position.`\n- For other intents, use a plain business-facing no-result statement for the requested scope and avoid technical wording such as `data is available`, `no matching data`, or similar phrasing.\n- If warnings materially affect trust, mention them briefly in the first text block only.\n- When returning a table, use the row objects from the normalized payload source named by the display plan table's `sourceRowKey`. Do not invent or rename columns, and do not add columns that are not already present in the provided rows.\n- When returning a table from the display plan, include the display plan table's `columns` array unchanged in the table block.\n- Use stable table headings so the formatter can apply the response table contract:\n  - `Cash Position by Legal Entity and Currency`\n  - `Top Accounts Driving Today's Position`\n  - `Cash Position for the Requested Legal Entity`\n  - `Cash Position for Bank Accounts`\n  - `Cash Position for the Requested Bank Account`\n  - `Bank Balance Details`\n  - `Cash Position Shortfall Accounts`\n  - `Surplus Accounts`\n  - `Intraday Statement Lines`\n- Use cash-position row currency from `Currency` and bank-balance row currency from `BalanceCurrency`; keep amount values numeric when they are numeric in the source rows.\n- In text blocks, render amount values as business-readable numbers with the currency code, not as raw numeric literals or exponential notation.\n- Show `SurplusOrDeficit` as a signed surplus or deficit value. Show `ShortfallAmount` as a positive shortfall amount.\n- Do not expose internal-only helper fields that begin with `_`.\n- Use `sequence` values that start at `1` and increase by `1` in output order.\n- If the user asks specifically about one current cash-position metric such as expected receipts, scheduled payments, opening balance, cleared receipts, cleared payments, intraday closing balance, target balance, or surplus / deficit, answer that metric first in the opening text block instead of leading with a generic cash-position summary.\n\n### Display-plan table behavior\n- After the first text block, add one table block for each item in `guarded display plan.tables`, in plan order.\n- For each display-plan table:\n  - Set `heading` to the plan table `heading`.\n  - Set `columns` to the plan table `columns`.\n  - Set `content` to the row array in `normalized result payload` named by the plan table `sourceRowKey`.\n  - Set `sequence` to the plan table `sequence` if present; otherwise continue the sequence after the text block.\n- If `guarded display plan.tables` is empty, do not add a table.\n- Do not add extra tables beyond the guarded display plan.\n\n### Intent-specific behavior\n- For `Get_overall_current_cash_position`:\n  - The first text block should summarize the strongest and weakest current-day positions using only facts that are directly supported by `normalized result payload.cashPositionSummaryRows`.\n  - Keep the overall headline to two or three short complete sentences.\n  - The overall headline must mention exactly two scoped positions:\n    - the one summary row with the highest `FinalCashPosition`\n    - the one summary row with the lowest `FinalCashPosition`\n  - Do not add extra entity-level callouts beyond those two scoped positions.\n  - If you include a third sentence, use it only for one target-status fact tied to either the strongest row or the weakest row.\n  - If you add a sentence about target position, write it as a standalone sentence with the full subject, for example `[Legal Entity] [Currency] is 395,424,693.60 USD above target.` Never omit the verb `is`.\n  - If the weakest row has no target balance, say that plainly instead of inventing a target comparison.\n  - When you mention a surplus, deficit, or below-target condition, it must match the `SurplusOrDeficit` value visible in the summary rows for that legal entity and currency.\n  - Do not describe a legal entity or currency as below target when the visible summary row shows a positive surplus value, and do not describe it as surplus when the visible summary row shows a negative deficit value.\n  - Do not use `normalized result payload.cashPositionTopContributorRows` to make a conflicting entity-level summary statement.\n  - Add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - `Unassigned` account rows must not be called out in the top-drivers table or in the first summary paragraph for this overall view.\n  - Add an `actions` block with:\n    - `Show the current cash position in MXN for the legal entity Vision Mexico`\n    - `Show the current cash position in USD for the bank account BofA-458`\n    - `Which accounts are below target right now?`\n- For `Get_current_cash_position_by_legal_entity`:\n  - The first text block should summarize the requested legal entity and currency only.\n  - If the user specifically asked about expected receipts or scheduled payments, answer that requested metric first for the requested legal entity and currency.\n  - If you mention target position, write it as `[Legal Entity] [Currency] is X above target.` or `[Legal Entity] [Currency] is X below target.`\n  - Add tables from the guarded display plan.\n- For `Get_current_cash_position_by_bank_account`:\n  - The first text block should summarize the requested bank account and currency only.\n  - If the user specifically asked about expected receipts or scheduled payments, answer that requested metric first for the requested bank account and currency.\n  - If you mention target position, write it as `[Bank Account] [Currency] at [Bank] is X above target.` or `[Bank Account] [Currency] at [Bank] is X below target.`\n  - Add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - Do not add a line-item drill-down table in this increment.\n- For `Get_balance_shortfall_details`:\n  - Use `normalized result payload.shortfallRows` as the table source.\n  - Summarize total shortfall pressure and the one or two most material impacted accounts only.\n  - If shortfall rows exist, add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - If shortfall rows exist, include an `actions` block with:\n    - `Review Shortfall Drivers for Impacted Accounts`\n    - `Show surplus accounts that could be reviewed`\n- For `Get_surplus_balance_accounts`:\n  - Use `normalized result payload.rows` as the table source. These rows are the top surplus accounts by positive surplus amount.\n  - Start by stating that the workflow can review surplus balances but does not recommend, initiate, or execute transfers.\n  - Summarize the largest one or two surplus accounts only.\n  - If rows exist, add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - Do not generate source-to-destination transfer proposals, transfer legs, recommended transfer amounts, policy eligibility statements, rule priority, cut-off guidance, approval guidance, FX handling, or execution next steps.\n  - If no surplus rows exist, return only one `text` block that says no surplus accounts are currently available for the requested scope.\n- For `Get_intra-day_details`:\n  - If `validation result.selectedRoute` or `normalized result payload.route` is `INTRADAY_SCOPE_DISCOVERY`, return only one `text` block for account selection or no impacted account detection. Do not add tables or actions for this route.\n  - If `normalized result payload.requiresAccountSelection` is `true`, ask the user to choose one impacted account from `normalized result payload.impactedAccounts`.\n  - When asking for account selection, mention only account identifiers from `normalized result payload.impactedAccounts`; do not summarize shortfall totals or individual shortfall amounts.\n  - If no bank account was supplied and `normalized result payload.hasShortfallAccounts` is `false`, return only one `text` block explaining that no currently impacted shortfall account was detected in the current position to drill into.\n  - If `normalized result payload.hasResults` is `true`, summarize the main intraday inflow or outflow using only `normalized result payload.intradayNetFlowDirection` and `normalized result payload.intradayNetFlowAmount`; do not calculate net flow from table rows.\n  - If `intradayNetFlowDirection` is `OUTFLOW`, say the selected account shows a net outflow of `intradayNetFlowAmount` in the row currency. If it is `INFLOW`, say net inflow. If it is `NEUTRAL`, say inflows and outflows are balanced.\n  - Add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - When intraday rows exist, include an `actions` block with:\n    - `Show surplus accounts that could be reviewed`\n- For existing bank-balance intents:\n  - Keep the existing inquiry-oriented behavior.\n  - Summarize the most decision-useful takeaway first instead of repeating each row in prose.\n  - If rows are available, add tables from the guarded display plan.\n  - If no rows are available, say that no balance data is currently available for the requested scope and stop there.\n\n### Hard constraints\n- Treat the validation result as the source of truth for whether the request can execute.\n- For executable requests, use only facts present in the normalized result payload.\n- Do not invent totals, dates, balances, legal entities, banks, accounts, or currencies.\n- Do not invent categories, severity bands, summaries, or next steps that are not grounded in the normalized result payload.\n- Never claim that a transfer was recommended, created, initiated, confirmed, submitted, executed, or handed off.\n- Do not return a top-level object with fields such as `agent`, `intent`, `schema_version`, `title`, `description`, `timestamp`, `topicName`, or `agent_response`.\n- Return only the JSON array of blocks described above.\n- Do not generate markdown."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"oneOf\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"text\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 1\n          },\n          \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type\",\n          \"content\",\n          \"sequence\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"table\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"heading\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"columns\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"additionalProperties\": {\n                \"type\": [\n                  \"string\",\n                  \"number\",\n                  \"boolean\",\n                  \"null\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type\",\n          \"heading\",\n          \"content\",\n          \"sequence\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"actions\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"minItems\": 1\n          },\n          \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type\",\n          \"content\",\n          \"sequence\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Normalize Cash Position Results",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const tryParseJson = (value) => {\n  if (typeof value !== \"string\") {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(value);\n  } catch (e) {\n    return value;\n  }\n};\n\nconst isObject = (value) => value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\nconst isNonEmptyString = (value) => typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim().length > 0;\n\nconst normalizeStringArray = (value) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  return value\n    .filter(isNonEmptyString)\n    .map((item) => item.trim());\n};\n\nconst normalizeIntegerOrNull = (value) => (Number.isInteger(value) ? value : null);\nconst normalizeNumberOrNull = (value) => {\n  if (typeof value === \"number\") {\n    return Number.isFinite(value) ? value : null;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim().length) {\n    const numericValue = Number(value.replace(/,/g, \"\"));\n    return Number.isFinite(numericValue) ? numericValue : null;\n  }\n\n  return null;\n};\n\nconst roundMoney = (value) => {\n  const numericValue = normalizeNumberOrNull(value);\n  if (numericValue === null) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return Math.round(numericValue * 100) / 100;\n};\n\nconst toRowArray = (payload) => {\n  const normalized = tryParseJson(payload);\n\n  if (Array.isArray(normalized)) {\n    return normalized.filter(isObject);\n  }\n\n  if (!isObject(normalized)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const arrayKeys = [\"items\", \"rows\", \"data\", \"results\", \"records\"];\n  for (let i = 0; i < arrayKeys.length; i += 1) {\n    const candidate = normalized[arrayKeys[i]];\n    if (Array.isArray(candidate)) {\n      return candidate.filter(isObject);\n    }\n    if (isObject(candidate) && Array.isArray(candidate.items)) {\n      return candidate.items.filter(isObject);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return [normalized];\n};\n\nconst normalizeText = (value) => {\n  if (value === null || value === undefined) {\n    return \"\";\n  }\n\n  return String(value).trim().toLowerCase();\n};\n\nconst matchesAny = (candidate, filters) => {\n  if (!filters.length) {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  const normalizedCandidate = normalizeText(candidate);\n  if (!normalizedCandidate) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  return filters.some((filterValue) => normalizeText(filterValue) === normalizedCandidate);\n};\n\nconst unwrapNodeOutput = (value) => {\n  const normalized = tryParseJson(value);\n\n  if (isObject(normalized) && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(normalized, \"result\")) {\n    return normalized.result;\n  }\n\n  return normalized;\n};\n\nconst getNodeOutput = (nodeCode) => {\n  const node = $context.$nodes[nodeCode];\n  return node ? unwrapNodeOutput(node.$output) : null;\n};\n\nconst validationResult = getNodeOutput(\"VALIDATE_CASH_POSITION_REQUEST\") || {};\nconst extractedFilters = getNodeOutput(\"CASH_POSITION_SCOPE_EXTRACTOR\") || {};\n\nconst selectedQueryCode = isNonEmptyString(validationResult.selectedQueryCode)\n  ? validationResult.selectedQueryCode.trim()\n  : \"GETALLBANKBALANCES\";\nconst selectedRoute = isNonEmptyString(validationResult.selectedRoute)\n  ? validationResult.selectedRoute.trim()\n  : \"BALANCE_INQUIRY\";\n\nconst resolvedIntent = isNonEmptyString(validationResult.resolvedIntent)\n  ? validationResult.resolvedIntent.trim()\n  : (isNonEmptyString(extractedFilters.intent) ? extractedFilters.intent.trim() : \"Clarify_request\");\n\nconst resolvedFilters = isObject(validationResult.resolvedFilters)\n  ? validationResult.resolvedFilters\n  : extractedFilters;\n\nconst appliedFilters = {\n  intent: resolvedIntent,\n  legalEntities: normalizeStringArray(resolvedFilters.legalEntities),\n  banks: normalizeStringArray(resolvedFilters.banks),\n  bankAccounts: normalizeStringArray(resolvedFilters.bankAccounts),\n  currencies: normalizeStringArray(resolvedFilters.currencies),\n  staleBalanceOlderThanDays: normalizeIntegerOrNull(resolvedFilters.staleBalanceOlderThanDays),\n  requiresStaleBalanceCheck: resolvedFilters.requiresStaleBalanceCheck === true\n};\n\nconst currentCashPositionQueryCodes = [\n  \"GETOVERALLCURRENTCASHPOSITION\",\n  \"GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYLEGALENTITY\",\n  \"GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYBANKACCOUNT\"\n];\n\nconst queryNodeMap = {\n  GETOVERALLCURRENTCASHPOSITION: \"GETCURRENTCASHPOSITION\",\n  GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYLEGALENTITY: \"GETCURRENTCASHPOSITION\",\n  GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYBANKACCOUNT: \"GETCURRENTCASHPOSITION\",\n  GETALLBANKBALANCES: \"GETALLBANKBALANCES\",\n  GETBALANCESBYLEGALENTITY: \"GETBALANCESBYLEGALENTITY\",\n  GETBALANCESBYBANK: \"GETBALANCESBYBANK\",\n  GETBALANCESBYCURRENCY: \"GETBALANCESBYCURRENCY\",\n  GETSPECIFICBANKACCOUNTBALANCE: \"GETSPECIFICBANKACCOUNTBALANCE\",\n  GETSTALEORMISSINGBANKBALANCES: \"GETSTALEORMISSINGBANKBALANCES\",\n  GETBALANCEVARIANCEVIEW: \"GETBALANCEVARIANCEVIEW\",\n  GETINTRADAYDETAILS: \"GETINTRADAYDETAILS\"\n};\n\nconst queryCapabilities = {\n  GETOVERALLCURRENTCASHPOSITION: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: false,\n    bankAccounts: true,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYLEGALENTITY: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: false,\n    bankAccounts: true,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETCURRENTCASHPOSITIONBYBANKACCOUNT: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: false,\n    bankAccounts: true,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETALLBANKBALANCES: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: true,\n    bankAccounts: true,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETBALANCESBYLEGALENTITY: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: false,\n    bankAccounts: false,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETBALANCESBYBANK: {\n    legalEntities: false,\n    banks: true,\n    bankAccounts: false,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETBALANCESBYCURRENCY: {\n    legalEntities: false,\n    banks: false,\n    bankAccounts: false,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETSPECIFICBANKACCOUNTBALANCE: {\n    legalEntities: true,\n    banks: true,\n    bankAccounts: true,\n    currencies: true\n  },\n  GETSTALEORMISSINGBA