              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are Build Cash Position Display Plan.\n\nYour job is to choose the table display plan for the Cash Position Inquiry Assistant.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. Do not include markdown or explanatory text.\n\n### Input contract\nUse only:\n- validation result: {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_CASH_POSITION_REQUEST.$output.result}}\n- normalized result payload: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CASH_POSITION_RESULTS.$output.result}}\n- configured display table contracts: {{$context.$variables.cashPositionDisplayTableContracts}}\n- configured display table defaults: {{$context.$variables.cashPositionDisplayTableDefaults}}\n\n### Output contract\nReturn exactly one JSON object:\n{\n  \"context\": {\n    \"singleExplicitLegalEntity\": true,\n    \"explicitLegalEntity\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"tables\": [\n    {\n      \"heading\": \"string\",\n      \"sourceRowKey\": \"string\",\n      \"contractKey\": \"string\",\n      \"columns\": [\"FieldName\"],\n      \"sequence\": 2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notesForSummary\": [\"string\"]\n}\n\n### Available source row keys\nUse only source row keys present in the normalized result payload:\n- `rows`\n- `cashPositionSummaryRows`\n- `cashPositionAccountRows`\n- `cashPositionTopContributorRows`\n- `shortfallRows`\n- `surplusRows`\n\n### Context rules\n- `singleExplicitLegalEntity` is true only when `normalized result payload.appliedFilters.legalEntities` contains exactly one value.\n- `explicitLegalEntity` is that value when `singleExplicitLegalEntity` is true; otherwise it is an empty string.\n- When `singleExplicitLegalEntity` is true, omit `LegalEntity` from table columns because the table is already in that legal-entity context.\n- When `singleExplicitLegalEntity` is false, include `LegalEntity` when it is present in the chosen source rows.\n\n### Column rules\n- Preserve source field names exactly. Do not invent field names.\n- Do not include fields that begin with `_`.\n- Prefer business-facing, compact tables over dumping every available field.\n- Do not include `LegalEntityId`, `LastRefreshTime`, `IntradayStatementFlag`, or `MultiCurrencyAllowedFlag` unless the user explicitly asks for technical or identifier details.\n- Keep amount and date source values unchanged; a later formatter applies UI templates.\n\n### Contract rules\n- When validation result `selectedRoute` is `INTRADAY_SCOPE_DISCOVERY`, return an empty `tables` array. This route is for selecting one account before showing intraday details.\n- When a table matches one of the configured display table defaults, include its configured `contractKey`.\n- For known current table families, prefer the configured contract over a compact custom column set.\n- For future or unknown table shapes, omit `contractKey` and choose columns from the available source row fields.\n- The guardrail node may replace columns with the configured contract when `contractKey` is present or when the table heading and source row key match a configured default.\n\n### Current table defaults\n- For `Get_overall_current_cash_position`, include:\n  - `Cash Position by Legal Entity and Currency` from `cashPositionSummaryRows` with `contractKey` `cashPositionSummary`\n  - `Top Accounts Driving Today's Position` from `cashPositionTopContributorRows` with `contractKey` `cashPositionAccount`\n- For `Get_current_cash_position_by_legal_entity`, include:\n  - `Cash Position for the Requested Legal Entity` from `cashPositionSummaryRows` with `contractKey` `cashPositionSummary`\n  - `Cash Position for Bank Accounts` from `cashPositionAccountRows` with `contractKey` `cashPositionAccount`\n- For `Get_current_cash_position_by_bank_account`, include:\n  - `Cash Position for the Requested Bank Account` from `rows` with `contractKey` `cashPositionAccount`\n- For `Get_all_bank_balances`, include exactly one table:\n  - `Bank Balance Details` from `rows` with `contractKey` `bankBalanceDetail`\n  - Do not add `surplusRows` or `shortfallRows` tables for this intent. Surplus and shortfall can be mentioned in summary text, but separate filtered tables belong only to the surplus or shortfall intents.\n- For `Get_balance_shortfall_details`, include:\n  - `Cash Position Shortfall Accounts` from `shortfallRows` with `contractKey` `shortfallAccounts`\n- For `Get_surplus_balance_accounts`, include:\n  - `Surplus Accounts` from `rows` with `contractKey` `surplusAccounts`\n- For `Get_intra-day_details`, include:\n  - `Intraday Statement Lines` from `rows` with `contractKey` `intradayStatementLines`\n- For `Get_balances_by_bank`, include:\n  - `Bank Balance Summary` from `rows` with `contractKey` `bankBalanceByBankSummary`\n- For `Get_balances_by_currency`, include:\n  - `Bank Balance Summary by Currency` from `rows` with `contractKey` `bankBalanceByCurrencySummary`\n- For `Get_specific_bank_account_balance`, include:\n  - `Bank Balance Details` from `rows` with `contractKey` `bankBalanceDetail`\n- For account-level bank-balance intents, include:\n  - `Bank Balance Details` from `rows` with `contractKey` `bankBalanceDetail`\n- Use `cashPositionAccount` only for current-cash-position rows with cash-position fields such as `OpeningBalance`, `ExpectedReceipts`, `ScheduledPayments`, and `FinalCashPosition`.\n- Do not use `bankBalanceByBankSummary` or `bankBalanceByCurrencySummary` when source rows contain account-level fields such as `BankAccount`, `BalanceAmount`, `BankBranch`, `TargetBalance`, or `VarianceAmount`.\n\n### Hard constraints\n- Only include a table when its source row key contains at least one row.\n- Use `sequence` values that leave room for the opening text block. The first table should use sequence `2`, then increment by `1`.\n- If no table should be displayed, return an empty `tables` array.\n- Do not mention internal workflow names or validation mechanics in `notesForSummary`."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"context\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"singleExplicitLegalEntity\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"explicitLegalEntity\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"singleExplicitLegalEntity\",\n        \"explicitLegalEntity\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"heading\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"sourceRowKey\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"columns\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          },\n          \"contractKey\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"heading\",\n          \"sourceRowKey\",\n          \"columns\",\n          \"sequence\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"notesForSummary\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"context\",\n    \"tables\",\n    \"notesForSummary\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Guard Cash Position Display Plan",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const tryParseJson = (value) => {\n  if (typeof value !== \"string\") {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(value);\n  } catch (e) {\n    return value;\n  }\n};\n\nconst isObject = (value) => value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\n\nconst unwrapNodeOutput = (value) => {\n  const normalized = tryParseJson(value);\n\n  if (isObject(normalized) && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(normalized, \"result\")) {\n    return normalized.result;\n  }\n\n  return normalized;\n};\n\nconst getNodeOutput = (nodeCode) => {\n  const node = $context.$nodes[nodeCode];\n  return node ? unwrapNodeOutput(node.$output) : null;\n};\n\nconst normalizeStringArray = (value) => (\n  Array.isArray(value)\n    ? value.filter((item) => typeof item === \"string\" && item.trim().length).map((item) => item.trim())\n    : []\n);\n\nconst normalizedResult = getNodeOutput(\"NORMALIZE_CASH_POSITION_RESULTS\") || {};\nconst validationResult = getNodeOutput(\"VALIDATE_CASH_POSITION_REQUEST\") || {};\nconst rawPlan = getNodeOutput(\"BUILD_CASH_POSITION_DISPLAY_PLAN\");\nconst parsedPlan = tryParseJson(rawPlan);\nconst loadedDisplayContracts = getNodeOutput(\"LOAD_CASH_POSITION_DISPLAY_CONTRACTS\") || {};\nconst workflowVariables = isObject($context.$variables) ? $context.$variables : {};\nconst configuredTableContracts = isObject(workflowVariables.cashPositionDisplayTableContracts)\n  ? workflowVariables.cashPositionDisplayTableContracts\n  : isObject(loadedDisplayContracts.tableContracts)\n    ? loadedDisplayContracts.tableContracts\n    : {};\nconst configuredTableDefaults = isObject(workflowVariables.cashPositionDisplayTableDefaults)\n  ? workflowVariables.cashPositionDisplayTableDefaults\n  : isObject(loadedDisplayContracts.tableDefaults)\n    ? loadedDisplayContracts.tableDefaults\n    : {};\n\nconst appliedFilters = isObject(normalizedResult.appliedFilters) ? normalizedResult.appliedFilters : {};\nconst legalEntities = normalizeStringArray(appliedFilters.legalEntities);\nconst singleExplicitLegalEntity = legalEntities.length === 1;\nconst explicitLegalEntity = singleExplicitLegalEntity ? legalEntities[0] : \"\";\nconst selectedRoute = typeof validationResult.selectedRoute === \"string\" ? validationResult.selectedRoute : \"\";\nconst suppressTablesForRoute = selectedRoute === \"INTRADAY_SCOPE_DISCOVERY\";\n\nconst tableSources = {\n  rows: normalizedResult.rows,\n  cashPositionSummaryRows: normalizedResult.cashPositionSummaryRows,\n  cashPositionAccountRows: normalizedResult.cashPositionAccountRows,\n  cashPositionTopContributorRows: normalizedResult.cashPositionTopContributorRows,\n  shortfallRows: normalizedResult.shortfallRows,\n  surplusRows: normalizedResult.surplusRows\n};\n\nconst hasRows = (sourceRowKey) => Array.isArray(tableSources[sourceRowKey]) && tableSources[sourceRowKey].length > 0;\n\nconst contractColumns = (contractKey) => {\n  if (typeof contractKey !== \"string\" || !contractKey.trim().length) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const configuredColumns = configuredTableContracts[contractKey.trim()];\n  return Array.isArray(configuredColumns) ? configuredColumns.slice() : [];\n};\n\nconst sourceFields = (sourceRowKey) => {\n  const rows = Array.isArray(tableSources[sourceRowKey]) ? tableSources[sourceRowKey] : [];\n  const fields = [];\n  rows.forEach((row) => {\n    if (!isObject(row)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    Object.keys(row).forEach((field) => {\n      if (fields.indexOf(field) === -1) {\n        fields.push(field);\n      }\n    });\n  });\n  return fields;\n};\n\nconst knownDefaultByHeadingAndSource = () => {\n  const index = {};\n\n  Object.keys(configuredTableDefaults).forEach((key) => {\n    const defaults = configuredTableDefaults[key];\n    if (!Array.isArray(defaults)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    defaults.forEach((table) => {\n      if (!isObject(table) || typeof table.heading !== \"string\" || typeof table.sourceRowKey !== \"string\") {\n        return;\n      }\n      index[`${table.heading.trim()}||${table.sourceRowKey.trim()}`] = table;\n    });\n  });\n\n  return index;\n};\n\nconst defaultContractIndex = knownDefaultByHeadingAndSource();\nconst forceConfiguredDefaultIntents = [\n  \"Get_intra-day_details\",\n  \"Get_balances_by_bank\",\n  \"Get_balances_by_currency\"\n];\nconst aggregateBankBalanceContractKeys = [\n  \"bankBalanceByBankSummary\",\n  \"bankBalanceByCurrencySummary\"\n];\nconst aggregateBankBalanceFields = [\n  \"BankAccountCount\",\n  \"LegalEntityCount\",\n  \"BankCount\",\n  \"TotalBalanceAmount\",\n  \"TotalTargetBalance\",\n  \"TotalVarianceAmount\",\n  \"LatestBalanceDate\"\n];\nconst compatibleBankBalanceDetailContractKeys = [\n  \"\",\n  \"bankBalanceDetail\"\n];\n\nconst fallbackTables = () => {\n  const intent = typeof validationResult.resolvedIntent === \"string\" ? validationResult.resolvedIntent : \"\";\n  const queryCode = typeof normalizedResult.queryCode === \"string\"\n    ? normalizedResult.queryCode\n    : (typeof validationResult.selectedQueryCode === \"string\" ? validationResult.selectedQueryCode : \"\");\n  if (Array.isArray(configuredTableDefaults[intent])) {\n    return configuredTableDefaults[intent];\n  }\n\n  if (queryCode !== \"CLARIFY_REQUEST\" && queryCode !== \"OFF_TOPIC_REQUEST\" && Array.isArray(configuredTableDefaults.bankBalanceDefault)) {\n    return configuredTableDefaults.bankBalanceDefault;\n  }\n\n  return [];\n};\n\nconst sanitizeColumns = (sourceRowKey, columns, allowConfiguredColumns) => {\n  const availableFields = sourceFields(sourceRowKey);\n  const availableSet = new Set(availableFields);\n  const sourceHasLegalEntity = availableSet.has(\"LegalEntity\") || columns.indexOf(\"LegalEntity\") !== -1;\n  const sanitized = [];\n\n  columns.forEach((field) => {\n    if (typeof field !== \"string\" || !field.trim().length) {\n      return;\n    }\n    const normalizedField = field.trim();\n    if (normalizedField.charAt(0) === \"_\") {\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!allowConfiguredColumns && !availableSet.has(normalizedField)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    if (normalizedField === \"LegalEntity\" && singleExplicitLegalEntity) {\n      return;\n    }\n    if (sanitized.indexOf(normalizedField) === -1) {\n      sanitized.push(normalizedField);\n    }\n  });\n\n  if (!singleExplicitLegalEntity && sourceHasLegalEntity && sanitized.indexOf(\"LegalEntity\") === -1) {\n    sanitized.unshift(\"LegalEntity\");\n  }\n\n  return sanitized;\n};\n\nconst defaultBankBalanceDetailTable = () => {\n  const defaults = configuredTableDefaults.bankBalanceDefault;\n  return Array.isArray(defaults) && isObject(defaults[0]) ? defaults[0] : null;\n};\n\nconst isIntradayDetailContext = () => (\n  selectedRoute === \"INTRADAY_DETAILS\" ||\n  (typeof validationResult.resolvedIntent === \"string\" && validationResult.resolvedIntent === \"Get_intra-day_details\") ||\n  (typeof normalizedResult.intent === \"string\" && normalizedResult.intent === \"Get_intra-day_details\")\n);\n\nconst isAccountLevelBankBalanceSource = (sourceRowKey) => {\n  if (isIntradayDetailContext()) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const availableSet = new Set(sourceFields(sourceRowKey));\n  return (\n    availableSet.has(\"BankAccount\") &&\n    availableSet.has(\"Bank\") &&\n    availableSet.has(\"BalanceCurrency\") &&\n    (availableSet.has(\"BalanceAmount\") || availableSet.has(\"LastKnownBalanceDate\"))\n  );\n};\n\nconst usesAggregateBankBalanceShape = (contractKey, columns) => {\n  if (aggregateBankBalanceContractKeys.indexOf(contractKey) !== -1) {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  return Array.isArray(columns) && columns.some((field) => aggregateBankBalanceFields.indexOf(field) !== -1);\n};\n\nconst usesIncompatibleBankBalanceContract = (contractKey, columns) => {\n  if (compatibleBankBalanceDetailContractKeys.indexOf(contractKey) === -1) {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  return usesAggregateBankBalanceShape(contractKey, columns);\n};\n\nconst sanitizeTables = (tables) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(tables)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const sanitizedTables = [];\n  tables.forEach((table) => {\n    if (!isObject(table)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    const sourceRowKey = typeof table.sourceRowKey === \"string\" ? table.sourceRowKey.trim() : \"\";\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(tableSources, sourceRowKey) || !hasRows(sourceRowKey)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    const fallbackFields = sourceFields(sourceRowKey).filter((field) => field.charAt(0) !== \"_\");\n    let heading = typeof table.heading === \"string\" && table.heading.trim().length\n      ? table.heading.trim()\n      : \"Cash Position Details\";\n    let contractKey = typeof table.contractKey === \"string\" && table.contractKey.trim().length\n      ? table.contractKey.trim()\n      : (isObject(defaultContractIndex[`${heading}||${sourceRowKey}`]) ? defaultContractIndex[`${heading}||${sourceRowKey}`].contractKey : \"\");\n    const requestedColumns = Array.isArray(table.columns) && table.columns.length ? table.columns : fallbackFields;\n    if (isAccountLevelBankBalanceSource(sourceRowKey) && usesIncompatibleBankBalanceContract(contractKey, requestedColumns)) {\n      const detailDefault = defaultBankBalanceDetailTable();\n      if (detailDefault) {\n        heading = typeof detailDefault.heading === \"string\" && detailDefault.heading.trim().length\n          ? detailDefault.heading.trim()\n          : heading;\n        contractKey = typeof detailDefault.contractKey === \"string\" && detailDefault.contractKey.trim().length\n          ? detailDefault.contractKey.trim()\n          : \"bankBalanceDetail\";\n      }\n    }\n    const configuredColumns = contractColumns(contractKey);\n    const rawColumns = configuredColumns.length\n      ? configuredColumns\n      : requestedColumns;\n    const columns = sanitizeColumns(sourceRowKey, rawColumns, configuredColumns.length > 0);\n    if (!columns.length) {\n      return;\n    }\n    sanitizedTables.push({\n      heading,\n      sourceRowKey,\n      contractKey,\n      columns,\n      sequence: sanitizedTables.length + 2\n    });\n  });\n\n  return sanitizedTables;\n};\n\nconst intent = typeof validationResult.resolvedIntent === \"string\" ? validationResult.resolvedIntent : \"\";\nconst shouldForceConfiguredDefaults = forceConfiguredDefaultIntents.indexOf(intent) !== -1;\nconst llmTables = isObject(parsedPlan) && !shouldForceConfiguredDefaults && !suppressTablesForRoute ? sanitizeTables(parsedPlan.tables) : [];\nconst fallbackDisplayTables = suppressTablesForRoute ? [] : sanitizeTables(fallbackTables());\nconst tables = suppressTablesForRoute ? [] : (llmTables.length ? llmTables : fallbackDisplayTables);\nconst notesForSummary = isObject(parsedPlan) && Array.isArray(parsedPlan.notesForSummary)\n  ? parsedPlan.notesForSummary.filter((item) => typeof item === \"string\" && item.trim().length).map((item) => item.trim())\n  : [];\n\nreturn {\n  context: {\n    singleExplicitLegalEntity,\n    explicitLegalEntity\n  },\n  tables,\n  notesForSummary,\n  usedFallback: !llmTables.length,\n  forcedConfiguredDefaults: shouldForceConfiguredDefaults,\n  suppressedTablesForRoute: suppressTablesForRoute ? selectedRoute : \"\"\n};"
          },
